[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
**Short answer**

*Use a **`color‑relief`** layer.*  
Its only paint property that matters is **`color‑relief‑color`**, which must be an `interpolate` expression that reads the elevation value with the special `["elevation"]` expression. The expression builds the hypsometric ramp (sea‑level blues → greens → browns → whites).

Below is a complete, copy‑and‑paste‑ready example that shows:

1. Adding the `raster-dem` source (your DEM tiles).  
2. Adding a `color‑relief` layer that tints the terrain by elevation.  
3. Optional tweaks (opacity, resampling, exaggeration, sky).

---

## 1. Add the DEM source

```js
// Assuming you already have a MapLibre map instance called `map`
map.addSource('terrain-dem', {
  type: 'raster-dem',
  // URL pattern that returns DEM tiles (Terrarium, Mapbox, etc.)
  url: 'https://my.tileserver.com/terrain/{z}/{x}/{y}.webp',
  // The encoding must match the tiles you serve (default is "mapbox")
  // encoding: 'terrarium',
  maxzoom: 12
});
```

> **Note** – The source is *only* a `raster-dem`. Do **not** add a `raster` layer for it; the `color‑relief` layer will read the elevation values directly from the source.

---

## 2. Add the `color‑relief` layer

```js
map.addLayer({
  id: 'hypsometric-tint',
  type: 'color-relief',          // <‑‑ THIS IS THE KEY
  source: 'terrain-dem',
  paint: {
    // 1️⃣ The ramp – an interpolate expression over ["elevation"]
    'color-relief-color': [
      'interpolate',
      ['linear'],                // linear interpolation between stops
      ['elevation'],             // special expression that returns meters
      // ── elevation (m) ──   ── colour ───────────────────────
      0,      '#2c7bb6',        // deep water – dark blue
      50,     '#3b8cc4',        // shallow water – lighter blue
      200,    '#5fa5d0',        // near‑shore – cyan‑green
      500,    '#7fc97f',        // lowlands – green
      1000,   '#c2e699',        // foothills – light green
      1500,   '#ffffbf',        // mid‑elevation – yellow‑ish
      2500,   '#fdae61',        // sub‑alpine – orange
      3500,   '#d73027',        // alpine – red‑brown
      4500,   '#ffffff'         // highest peaks – pure white
    ],

    // 2️⃣ Optional opacity (0‑1). 1 = fully opaque.
    'color-relief-opacity': 0.85,

    // 3️⃣ Optional resampling mode (GL JS 5.20+).  "linear" is the default.
    // 'resampling': 'linear'
  }
});
```

### How the ramp works

| Elevation (m) | Hex colour | Visual cue |
|---------------|------------|------------|
| **0**         | `#2c7bb6`  | Deep ocean (dark blue) |
| **50**        | `#3b8cc4`  | Shallow water (lighter blue) |
| **200**       | `#5fa5d0`  | Coast / estuary (cyan‑green) |
| **500**       | `#7fc97f`  | Lowland vegetation (green) |
| **1000**      | `#c2e699`  | Foothills (light green) |
| **1500**      | `#ffffbf`  | Transition zone (yellow) |
| **2500**      | `#fdae61`  | Sub‑alpine (orange) |
| **3500**      | `#d73027`  | Alpine rock (red‑brown) |
| **4500**      | `#ffffff`  | Snow‑capped peaks (white) |

You can add, remove, or move stops to suit your own colour palette. The expression is evaluated **client‑side** for every pixel that the DEM supplies, so no pre‑rendered coloured tiles are needed.

---

## 3. (Optional) Show the terrain in 3‑D and add a sky

If you also want a tilted 3‑D view, enable terrain and a sky background:

```js
// 3‑D terrain (exaggeration can be >1 if you want more dramatic relief)
map.setTerrain({ source: 'terrain-dem', exaggeration: 1.2 });

// Pitch the camera so you can see the relief
map.easeTo({ pitch: 60, bearing: 0, duration: 2000 });

// Add a sky – this is a *root‑level* object, not a layer
map.setSky({
  'sky-color': '#199EF3',
  'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,
  'horizon-color': '#ffffff',
  'horizon-fog-blend': 0.5,
  'fog-color': '#0000ff',
  'fog-ground-blend': 0.5
});
```

> **Important** – The sky only appears when `setTerrain()` is active (i.e., when you have a 3‑D mesh). If you keep the map flat (`pitch: 0`), the sky will simply fill the background.

---

## 4. Full minimal example (HTML + JS)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – Hypsometric Tint</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; padding:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {},          // we’ll add sources programmatically
      layers: []            // same for layers
    },
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2,
    pitch: 0,
    bearing: 0
  });

  map.on('load', () => {
    // 1️⃣ DEM source
    map.addSource('terrain-dem', {
      type: 'raster-dem',
      url: 'https://my.tileserver.com/terrain/{z}/{x}/{y}.webp',
      maxzoom: 12
    });

    // 2️⃣ Hypsometric tint
    map.addLayer({
      id: 'hypsometric-tint',
      type: 'color-relief',
      source: 'terrain-dem',
      paint: {
        'color-relief-color': [
          'interpolate',
          ['linear'],
          ['elevation'],
          0,    '#2c7bb6',
          50,   '#3b8cc4',
          200,  '#5fa5d0',
          500,  '#7fc97f',
          1000, '#c2e699',
          1500, '#ffffbf',
          2500, '#fdae61',
          3500, '#d73027',
          4500, '#ffffff'
        ],
        'color-relief-opacity': 0.85
      }
    });

    // 3️⃣ (optional) 3‑D terrain + sky
    map.setTerrain({ source: 'terrain-dem', exaggeration: 1.2 });
    map.easeTo({ pitch: 60, duration: 1500 });
    map.setSky({
      'sky-color': '#199EF3',
      'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,
      'horizon-color': '#ffffff',
      'horizon-fog-blend': 0.5,
      'fog-color': '#0000ff',
      'fog-ground-blend': 0.5
    });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

